                        "title":  "Updraft Gust",
                        "category":  "Hazards",
                        "summary":  "A sudden rising current pushes an airship above its intended altitude before the pilot can stabilize it.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Updraft gusts are brief but dangerous near crowded routes, overhead obstacles, storm layers, and islands with irregular wind patterns. A fast pilot response keeps the vessel from climbing into a worse hazard."
                                 ],
                        "sections":  [
                                         {
